{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For by the very thing that they plotted against them.</b> For He delivered the people by the very same thing that the Egyptians plotted against Israel — as in כִּי יָזִד אִישׁ עַל רֵעֵהוּ (Exodus 21:14). This was: He killed their firstborn, just as the Egyptians had killed every male born to Israel; He drowned them in the sea, just as they had drowned the sons in the Nile; and He killed the firstborn, corresponding to בְּנִי בְכֹרִי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Exodus 4:22), וַתְּמָאֵן לְשַׁלְּחוֹ (ibid.); and He hardened their heart after they refused to obey of their own will. In this He demonstrated His greatness above all elohim, for no nation imagined that any elohim — even the heavenly princes among their deities — could exact measure for measure in every respect; they thought it possible only in one particular thing peculiar to it alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:07.601480093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}